{"text": "Community Alliance Program: A Partnership for Youth\n\nRecognizing the value of community support in fostering better\nfamily communication on difficult issues, the Tobacco Institute\nis helping to make possible a program to build stronger\n\nfamilies and help young people make responsible decisions.\n\nThe project, known as the Community Alliance Program (CAP), is\nconducted by the National Association of State Boards of\nEducation (NASBE), and gives grants of $3,000 each to 20\ncommunities per year for the purpose of establishing or\nmaintaining local programs to unite communities in helping\n\nfamilies.\n\nLocal community projects often are supplemented by the two\ntobacco-funded NASBE booklets, Helping Youth Decide and Helping\nYouth Say No. More than 700,000 booklets have been distributed\n\nnationwide, \u2018many at Community Alliance Programs.\n\nCommunity representatives receive assistance from NASBE in\nstructuring their community plan, setting strategies, and\ntailoring the CAP program to the specific needs of the\ncommunity. Participants receive suggestions for seminars,\nworkshops, symposia and retreats -- ideas which will help them\n\nbuild a successful program back home.\n\nTIMN 0169299 ~", "words": [{"text": "Community", "x0": 168, "y0": 49, "x1": 249, "y1": 62, "conf": 95.0}, {"text": "Alliance", "x0": 259, "y0": 49, "x1": 330, "y1": 60, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "Program:", "x0": 341, "y0": 50, "x1": 410, "y1": 62, "conf": 95.0}, {"text": "A", "x0": 432, "y0": 50, "x1": 441, "y1": 59, "conf": 94.0}, {"text": "Partnership", "x0": 451, "y0": 49, "x1": 550, "y1": 63, "conf": 94.0}, {"text": "for", "x0": 562, "y0": 50, "x1": 586, "y1": 60, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "Youth", "x0": 597, "y0": 50, "x1": 642, "y1": 61, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "Recognizing", "x0": 118, "y0": 92, "x1": 217, "y1": 105, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "the", "x0": 228, "y0": 93, "x1": 253, "y1": 103, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "value", "x0": 264, "y0": 93, "x1": 307, "y1": 103, "con